{"c":[{"id":"78a720eef0312ba1","sum":"Helper tests: candidate generation stops at MAX_GENERATOR_VISITS, not time (stats.ms is diagnostic; a cap stop marks a partial window cut); close page sessions before Helper.shutdown and Store.close, or a trailing walk hits a closed store.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261008T122806Z-20adf579b39b18f9","text":"Candidate generation stops at MAX_GENERATOR_VISITS, not elapsed time; no setGeneratorClock, budgetMs or --generator-clock override remains. stats.ms is diagnostic, and a visit-cap stop still marks a partial window cut.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261008T131449Z-7a0add213d3fc6e0","text":"Tests that wire page sessions into Helper must close those sessions before Helper.shutdown and Store.close; a scheduled trailing walk otherwise reaches a closed store.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"71e3e7853f09b491","sum":"Oracle and choices: realfill-asks seals requests before the canned oracle answers, so FillTrace.owns(req) is false there; keep oracle rules off the trace. A source-supported choice needs its whole unit sent, so only Asks naming the source window get unit-based choices.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261008T143933Z-2d2e0e57729d25b3","text":"realfill-asks seals each request before the canned oracle answers it, so FillTrace.owns(req) is false there: the oracle reads fill questions by their text on the scoreboard but by the trace in the vs1 kit (runB31). Don't make oracle rules depend on the trace.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261008T143933Z-70fb13e0b1aaff9c","text":"v2/choices: a source-supported choice needs its whole unit sent; a TextEdit note never fits an Ask that does not name it (prose share keeps half back), so only Asks naming the source window get unit-based choices. The user's request is always a basis.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
